<h1>vertex</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
An item in a <a href="graph.html"><em>graph</em></a>.  Sometimes referred to as a <a href="node.html"><em>node</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Specialization</strong> (... is a kind of me.)<br>
<a href="cutvertex.html"><em>cut vertex</em></a>, <a href="freevertex.html"><em>free vertex</em></a>, <a href="matchedvertx.html"><em>matched vertex</em></a>, <a href="steinervertx.html"><em>Steiner vertex</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>Aggregate child</strong> (... is a part of or used in me.)<br>
<a href="indegree.html"><em>in-degree</em></a>, <a href="outdegree.html"><em>out-degree</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="edge.html"><em>edge</em></a>, <a href="vertexcolor.html"><em>vertex coloring</em></a>, <a href="vertexcover.html"><em>vertex cover</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
The plural is vertices.  Another plural is vertexes.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

